-- title:
--   Theorem 2, p. 25 — monotonicity of performance bounds: W^TS ≥ W^IRS.FH ≥ W^IRS.V-Zero and W^TS ≥ W^IRS.V-EMax
-- statement:
--   The model is the Bayesian bandit of §2.1: arms $a \in \mathcal A = \{1,\dots,K\}$ (0-based in Lean, $K \ge 1$), reward laws $\mathcal R_a(\theta_a)$, conjugate priors $\mathcal P_a(y_a)$, the Bayesian update $\mathcal U_a$, and the outcome law $\mathcal I(y)$ under which the arms are independent, $\theta_a \sim \mathcal P_a(y_a)$, and the rewards of arm $a$ are i.i.d. $\mathcal R_a(\theta_a)$ given $\theta_a$. The standing assumptions of §2.1 hold: $\mathcal U_a(y_a,r)$ is the Bayes posterior after observing $r$, the update maps are measurable, and $\mathbb E_{y_a}|R_{a,1}| < \infty$ for every belief $y_a$ (3).
--
--   For every horizon $T \in \mathbb N_0$ and belief vector $y$,
--
--   $$W^{TS}(T,y) \ge W^{IRS.FH}(T,y) \ge W^{IRS.V\text{-}Zero}(T,y) \tag{57}$$
--
--   and
--
--   $$W^{TS}(T,y) \ge W^{IRS.V\text{-}EMax}(T,y). \tag{58}$$
--
--   Here $W^{TS}(T,y) = \mathbb E_y[T \max_a \mu_a(\theta_a)]$ is the conventional regret benchmark, $W^{IRS.FH}$ and $W^{IRS.V\text{-}Zero}$ are the bounds (33) and (37), and $W^{IRS.V\text{-}EMax}$ is the penalised clairvoyant bound (19) with the penalty (26) generated by $W^{TS}$. IRS.FH and IRS.V-Zero thus monotonically tighten the upper bound on the Bayesian optimal performance, and IRS.V-EMax improves on the TS benchmark.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $W^{IRS.FH}$ is defined by its closed form (33). In $W^{IRS.V\text{-}EMax}$ the conditional expectations given $H_{t-1}$ in (26) are replaced by their conjugate closed forms ((36), (39)–(43)). At $T = 0$ all four bounds are $0$.
-- source:
--   Min, Maglaras, Moallemi, Thompson Sampling with Information Relaxation Penalties, arXiv:1902.04251v2, p. 25, Theorem 2, (57)–(58)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_InfoRelaxTS_Monotone_Setting

namespace InfoRelaxTS.Monotone

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

/-- Theorem 2 (monotonicity of performance bounds), p. 25, (57)–(58):
`W^TS(T, y) ≥ W^{IRS.FH}(T, y) ≥ W^{IRS.V-Zero}(T, y)` and `W^TS(T, y) ≥ W^{IRS.V-EMax}(T, y)`. -/
theorem theorem_2 {K : ℕ} [NeZero K] {Θ Y : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Θ] [StandardBorelSpace Θ]
    [Nonempty Θ] [MeasurableSpace Y]
    (R : Fin K → Kernel Θ ℝ) [∀ a, IsMarkovKernel (R a)]
    (P : Fin K → Kernel Y Θ) [∀ a, IsMarkovKernel (P a)]
    (U : Fin K → Y → ℝ → Y) (hM : StandingAssumptions R P U)
    (T : ℕ) (y : Fin K → Y) :
    WFH R P U T y ≤ WTS R P T y ∧ WVZ R P U T y ≤ WFH R P U T y ∧
      WVEMax R P U T y ≤ WTS R P T y := by sorry

end InfoRelaxTS.Monotone
